  "final_message": "{\"summary\":\"Implemented and verified `safeUploadPath`. It now validates the upload-client filename as one component, rejects non-string/empty values, NUL bytes, dot traversal, both separators, and Windows drive prefixes, then lexically resolves it under `baseDir` with a parent-containment check. Before, the function always threw TODO; now valid names return a destination path and invalid names throw. The `path.resolve`/`path.dirname` pairing provides lexical containment only. Truth status: verified. No meaningful implementation tasks remain.\",\"files_changed\":[\"src/upload-path.mjs\"],\"tests_run\":[\"`node --test` — passed 1/1\",\"Security matrix covering traversal, absolute paths, separators, drive-qualified names, NUL, empty, and non-string inputs — passed\",\"Git diff/scope check — unavailable because the fixture is not recognized as a Git repository; edits were made only through the scoped patch to `src/upload-path.mjs`\"],\"remaining_uncertainty\":[\"Symlink safety is intentionally outside this function. The downstream writer must use no-follow or equivalent exclusive-open semantics.\"]}",
